From d80206471150b1d9eaf9eb043b5170b675862ca8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lucascouts <lucascs@protonmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 11:29:17 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] agent_tasks_panel: left-aligned rows, a close button, a
 scrollbar, a text filter and multi-select

The Agent Tasks panel of 0035 (with 0039's labels, 0041's Open at Task and
0042's Delete) read badly once it filled up: row text was centred, there
was no scrollbar and no way to find a task by name, and acting on many
rows meant one click per row. Story 034.

Rows are drawn left-aligned. The open control is a ButtonLike given the
full width, and a ButtonLike with a width centres whatever it holds
(justify_center + text_center in crates/ui); the row now grows its inner
line to that width and holds the label in a flex line of its own, so the
text starts at the slot's left edge and only shrinks to truncate. The
progress text keeps the right end and is capped at 40% of the row, or on
a 320px dock it took every free pixel and the label had no slot to start
in. The group header's title takes the same Base04 inset ButtonLike gives
the rows, so the labels start under it. crates/ui is not touched.

A top toolbar carries an X ("Close Panel") that emits PanelEvent::Close,
which the dock honours only while it shows this panel -- the same rule as
the git panel. The operator's decision (2026-10-10): the X closes the
panel, not a row; there is no per-row close or dismiss. Nothing is reset
by it: toggles, filter text and selection are as they were on reopening.

The list gets a vertical scrollbar through ui::Scrollbars, settings-free
(the panel has no settings) and always shown while there is something to
scroll: Scrollbars::new hides the thumb a second after the pointer
enters, which the GUI proof caught as no scrollbar at all. A track runs
along it so a click on the track scrolls there.

A one-line input ("Filter tasks...") on the toolbar narrows the list to
rows whose label, description or thread title contains the text, case
insensitively and each field on its own, on top of the toggles. A header
is listed only with a listed row, counting those. A blank text is no
filter at all; with a real one and no match the panel says "No tasks
match the filter". Escape in the input clears it.

Rows can be selected: ctrl-click (cmd on macOS) toggles, shift-click takes
the listed rows from the anchor, neither opens the thread; a plain click
clears the selection and opens as before. agent_tasks_panel::ToggleSelected,
bound to shift-space in the AgentTasksPanel context of both default
keymaps, toggles the row one of whose controls has focus; outside a row it
propagates, so shift-space still types a space in the filter. Escape on the
panel clears the selection. A selected row draws element_selected as a
background -- never an extra line, which uniform_list's one-line height
forbids -- and says ", selected" to screen readers. The selection is keyed
by session and task id and dropped for any row that stops being listed.

Zed binds Tab to menu::SelectNext rather than to a focus move, and 0035's
panel never handled it, so its tab stops were out of the keyboard's reach
in the real app. The panel now maps SelectNext and SelectPrevious to
focus_next and focus_prev, as the elicitation card does.

While rows are selected a toolbar shows "N selected", Clear Selection,
Archive Selected (every selected ended, unarchived row in one batch;
running rows stay unarchived and selected) and, under the Archived filter,
Delete Selected through 0042's own prompt and store path: only the
selected archived rows are counted and deleted, never a thread, and only
the deleted records leave the selection -- a row selected meanwhile, or
one unarchived while the prompt was open, stays selected. A failed write
keeps memory and logs one line naming every id, as before.

While the text filter narrows the list, a group header's Archive acts on
what the header shows: only the group's listed rows that have ended
unarchived, never one a toggle or the text hides. With no text it archives
every finished task of the thread, as 0035 did.

It also runs rustfmt over four files of this crate that earlier patches
(0035-0042) shipped unformatted -- history_db.rs, its statement_tests.rs,
panel/delete_action_tests.rs and test_helpers.rs -- layout only, so that
cargo fmt --check -p agent_tasks_panel passes (the operator's decision,
2026-10-11).

No migration, no setting, no new crate, no store or database change.
Rides claude-agent-acp-plus BY DEPENDENCY after 0042, whose panel it
changes.

Story 064 (2026-11-02): test_helpers' AgentTask literal, which this patch
owns, gains `child_session_id: None` for the field 0056 adds later in the
series; the series is only ever built whole. No behaviour change.
---

